01a00eb7-6ee1-7439-8245-5a42f00930d5	2026-08-17 13:24:57.634498+05:30	2026-08-17 13:24:57.634498+05:30	prowler-azure-defender_ensure_iot_hub_defender_is_on-ab5c336b-0e6b-4d8b-bf82-45cc005163e1-global-ab5c336b-0e6b-4d8b-bf82-45cc005163e1	new	FAIL	No IoT Security Solutions found in the subscription Azure subscription 1 (ab5c336b-0e6b-4d8b-bf82-45cc005163e1).	high	high	\N	{}	defender_ensure_iot_hub_defender_is_on	{"risk": "Without **Defender for IoT**, device activity lacks telemetry and alerting, degrading CIA:\\n- Compromised devices join botnets and exfiltrate data\\n- Abused device identities alter cloud twins and commands\\n- Lateral movement from IoT networks to Azure workloads\\nThis blind spot increases dwell time and blast radius.", "notes": "Enabling Microsoft Defender for IoT will incur additional charges dependent on the level of usage.", "checkid": "defender_ensure_iot_hub_defender_is_on", "provider": "azure", "severity": "high", "checktype": [], "dependson": [], "relatedto": [], "categories": ["vulnerabilities"], "checktitle": "Defender for IoT Hub is set to On", "compliance": {"NIS2": ["3.6.2", "6.9.2"], "SOC2": ["cc_3_1", "cc_3_2", "cc_4_2", "cc_6_8", "cc_7_1"], "C5-2025": ["OPS-04.01B"], "CIS-2.0": ["2.2.1"], "CIS-2.1": ["2.2.1"], "CIS-3.0": ["3.2.1"], "CIS-4.0": ["9.2.1"], "CIS-5.0": ["8.2.1"], "CIS-6.0": ["8.2.1"], "ENS-RD2022": ["mp.s.4.r1.az.nt.3"], "MITRE-ATTACK": ["T1190", "T1486", "T1499"], "ISO27001-2022": ["A.5.19", "A.5.21", "A.5.25", "A.5.28", "A.5.29", "A.8.7", "A.8.9"], "FedRAMP-20x-KSI-Low-25.05C": ["ksi-inr"]}, "relatedurl": "", "description": "**Microsoft Defender for IoT security solution** exists in the subscription and reports status `Enabled` for monitored **IoT Hub** resources.", "remediation": {"code": {"cli": "", "other": "1. In the Azure portal, go to IoT hubs and open your hub\\n2. Select Defender for IoT > Overview\\n3. Click Secure your IoT solution and complete onboarding (select the hub if prompted)\\n4. If you see a toggle, set Enable Microsoft Defender for IoT to On and Save\\n5. Verify the IoT Security Solution shows as Enabled under Defender for IoT", "nativeiac": "```bicep\\n// Enable Defender for IoT by creating an IoT Security Solution\\nresource iotDefender 'Microsoft.Security/iotSecuritySolutions@2019-08-01' = {\\n  name: '<example_resource_name>'\\n  location: '<LOCATION>'\\n  properties: {\\n    displayName: '<example_resource_name>'\\n    iotHubs: ['<IOT_HUB_RESOURCE_ID>']  // CRITICAL: links the IoT Hub; creating this solution enables Defender for IoT\\n    status: 'Enabled'                   // CRITICAL: ensures the solution is enabled\\n  }\\n}\\n```", "terraform": "```hcl\\n# Enable Defender for IoT by creating an IoT Security Solution\\nresource \\"azurerm_iot_security_solution\\" \\"<example_resource_name>\\" {\\n  name                = \\"<example_resource_name>\\"\\n  resource_group_name = \\"<example_resource_name>\\"\\n  location            = \\"<LOCATION>\\"\\n  display_name        = \\"<example_resource_name>\\"\\n  iothub_ids          = [\\"<IOT_HUB_RESOURCE_ID>\\"]  # CRITICAL: links the IoT Hub; creating this solution enables Defender\\n}\\n```"}, "recommendation": {"url": "https://hub.prowler.com/check/defender_ensure_iot_hub_defender_is_on", "text": "Enable **Defender for IoT** on all IoT Hubs and keep it `Enabled`. Route security data to a central workspace and your SIEM. Apply **least privilege** to IoT identities, enforce **network segmentation** and private access, and use **defense in depth** with continuous monitoring, alert tuning, and periodic coverage reviews."}}, "servicename": "defender", "checkaliases": [], "resourcetype": "microsoft.security/iotsecuritysolutions", "resourcegroup": "security", "additionalurls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/defender-for-iot/device-builders/quickstart-onboard-iot-hub", "https://support.icompaas.com/support/solutions/articles/62000229850-ensure-that-microsoft-defender-for-iot-hub-is-set-to-on-"], "sub