01a00ec7-ded8-7e11-ac8b-fdfb331e3ca9	2026-08-17 13:42:54.873334+05:30	2026-08-17 13:42:54.873334+05:30	prowler-azure-app_ftp_deployment_disabled-ab5c336b-0e6b-4d8b-bf82-45cc005163e1-Central India-app-jaseflight-api-prod	new	PASS	FTP is disabled for app 'app-jaseflight-api-prod' in subscription 'Azure subscription 1 (ab5c336b-0e6b-4d8b-bf82-45cc005163e1)'.	high	high	\N	{}	app_ftp_deployment_disabled	{"risk": "Allowing **FTP (unencrypted)** exposes credentials on public endpoints, enabling **credential theft** and **session hijacking**.\\n\\nCompromise grants write access to code and content, enabling **malicious deployments**, backdoors, and data leakage, degrading **integrity** and **confidentiality**-with greater blast radius if shared, user-scope publishing credentials are used.", "notes": "Any deployment workflows that rely on FTP or FTPs rather than the WebDeploy or HTTPs endpoints may be affected.", "checkid": "app_ftp_deployment_disabled", "provider": "azure", "severity": "high", "checktype": [], "dependson": [], "relatedto": [], "categories": ["encryption"], "checktitle": "App Service web app has FTP disabled or FTPS-only enforced", "compliance": {"NIS2": ["5.1.2.a", "6.2.1", "6.2.2.b", "6.2.2.c"], "HIPAA": ["164_312_e_1"], "CIS-2.0": ["9.10"], "CIS-2.1": ["9.9"], "CIS-3.0": ["9.3"], "CCC-v2025.10": ["CCC.Core.CN01.AR01", "CCC.Core.CN01.AR03"], "SecNumCloud-3.2": ["10.2"], "ProwlerThreatScore-1.0": ["2.3.2"]}, "relatedurl": "", "description": "**Azure App Service web apps** are evaluated for **FTP exposure** via the `ftpsState` setting. Values `FtpsOnly` or `Disabled` indicate FTP is not allowed; `AllAllowed` means both FTP and FTPS are accepted.", "remediation": {"code": {"cli": "az webapp config set --resource-group <RESOURCE_GROUP> --name <APP_NAME> --ftps-state FtpsOnly", "other": "1. In Azure Portal, go to App Services and select your app\\n2. Go to Settings > Configuration > General settings\\n3. Set FTP state to FTPS only (or Disabled)\\n4. Click Save", "nativeiac": "```bicep\\n// Configure an existing App Service to enforce FTPS-only\\nresource webConfig 'Microsoft.Web/sites/config@2022-03-01' = {\\n  name: '<example_resource_name>/web'\\n  properties: {\\n    ftpsState: 'FtpsOnly' // CRITICAL: Sets FTP state to FTPS-only, avoiding insecure 'AllAllowed'\\n  }\\n}\\n```", "terraform": "```hcl\\n# Enforce FTPS-only on an App Service\\nresource \\"azurerm_windows_web_app\\" \\"<example_resource_name>\\" {\\n  name                = \\"<example_resource_name>\\"\\n  resource_group_name = \\"<example_resource_name>\\"\\n  location            = \\"<example_resource_name>\\"\\n  service_plan_id     = \\"<example_resource_id>\\"\\n\\n  site_config {\\n    ftps_state = \\"FtpsOnly\\" # CRITICAL: Enforces FTPS-only (not AllAllowed)\\n  }\\n}\\n```"}, "recommendation": {"url": "https://hub.prowler.com/check/app_ftp_deployment_disabled", "text": "Disable FTP or enforce **FTPS** (`ftpsState: FtpsOnly` or `Disabled`).\\n\\nPrefer **CI/CD** over manual FTP and apply **least privilege** with app-scoped credentials. Rotate publishing secrets, enforce modern TLS, and restrict access via private networking. *If FTP is unavoidable*, require FTPS and monitor publishing logs."}}, "servicename": "app", "checkaliases": [], "resourcetype": "microsoft.web/sites", "resourcegroup": "serverless", "additionalurls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/deploy-ftp?tabs=portal", "https://www.trendmicro.com/cloudoneconformity/knowledge-base/azure/AppService/ftp-access-disabled.html", "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-gb/answers/questions/1323820/can-i-create-an-azure-policy-that-disables-both-ft", "https://icompaas.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/62000234759-ensure-ftp-state-is-set-to-ftps-only-or-disabled-"], "subservicename": "", "resourceidtemplate": ""}	{}	01a00ec7-86e1-7a6c-8d5b-66e6a157f262	3e59acc5-3bdd-499e-8fd1-3e53b0a6ca47	2026-08-17 13:42:54.872207+05:30	f	{"NIS2": ["5.1.2.a", "6.2.1", "6.2.2.b", "6.2.2.c"], "HI