01a00ec8-39aa-796f-a660-0faa8d38a846	2026-08-17 13:43:18.123426+05:30	2026-08-17 13:43:18.123426+05:30	prowler-azure-defender_ensure_iot_hub_defender_is_on-ab5c336b-0e6b-4d8b-bf82-45cc005163e1-global-ab5c336b-0e6b-4d8b-bf82-45cc005163e1	\N	FAIL	No IoT Security Solutions found in the subscription Azure subscription 1 (ab5c336b-0e6b-4d8b-bf82-45cc005163e1).	high	high	\N	{}	defender_ensure_iot_hub_defender_is_on	{"risk": "Without **Defender for IoT**, device activity lacks telemetry and alerting, degrading CIA:\\n- Compromised devices join botnets and exfiltrate data\\n- Abused device identities alter cloud twins and commands\\n- Lateral movement from IoT networks to Azure workloads\\nThis blind spot increases dwell time and blast radius.", "notes": "Enabling Microsoft Defender for IoT will incur additional charges dependent on the level of usage.", "checkid": "defender_ensure_iot_hub_defender_is_on", "provider": "azure", "severity": "high", "checktype": [], "dependson": [], "relatedto": [], "categories": ["vulnerabilities"], "checktitle": "Defender for IoT Hub is set to On", "compliance": {"NIS2": ["3.6.2", "6.9.2"], "SOC2": ["cc_3_1", "cc_3_2", "cc_4_2", "cc_6_8", "cc_7_1"], "C5-2025": ["OPS-04.01B"], "CIS-2.0": ["2.2.1"], "CIS-2.1": ["2.2.1"], "CIS-3.0": ["3.2.1"], "CIS-4.0": ["9.2.1"], "CIS-5.0": ["8.2.1"], "CIS-6.0": ["8.2.1"], "ENS-RD2022": ["mp.s.4.r1.az.nt.3"], "MITRE-ATTACK": ["T1190", "T1486", "T1499"], "ISO27001-2022": ["A.5.19", "A.5.21", "A.5.25", "A.5.28", "A.5.29", "A.8.7", "A.8.9"], "FedRAMP-20x-KSI-Low-25.05C": ["ksi-inr"]}, "relatedurl": "", "description": "**Microsoft Defender for IoT security solution** exists in the subscription and reports status `Enabled` for monitored **IoT Hub** resources.", "remediation": {"code": {"cli": "", "other": "1. In the Azure portal, go to IoT hubs and open your hub\\n2. Select Defender for IoT > Overview\\n3. Click Secure your IoT solution and complete onboarding (select the hub if prompted)\\n4. If you see a toggle, set Enable Microsoft Defender for IoT to On and Save\\n5. Verify the IoT Security Solution shows as Enabled under Defender for IoT", "nativeiac": "```bicep\\n// Enable Defender for IoT by creating an IoT Security Solution\\nresource iotDefender 'Microsoft.Security/iotSecuritySolutions@2019-08-01' = {\\n  name: '<example_resource_name>'\\n  location: '<LOCATION>'\\n  properties: {\\n    displayName: '<example_resource_name>'\\n    iotHubs: ['<IOT_HUB_RESOURCE_ID>']  // CRITICAL: links the IoT Hub; creating this solution enables Defender for IoT\\n    status: 'Enabled'                   // CRITICAL: ensures the solution is enabled\\n  }\\n}\\n```", "terraform": "```hcl\\n# Enable Defender for IoT by creating an IoT Security Solution\\nresource \\"azurerm_iot_security_solution\\" \\"<example_resource_name>\\" {\\n  name                = \\"<example_resource_name>\\"\\n  resource_group_name = \\"<example_resource_name>\\"\\n  location            = \\"<LOCATION>\\"\\n  display_name        = \\"<example_resource_name>\\"\\n  iothub_ids          = [\\"<IOT_HUB_RESOURCE_ID>\\"]  # CRITICAL: links the IoT Hub; creating this solution enables Defender\\n}\\n```"}, "recommendation": {"url": "https://hub.prowler.com/check/defender_ensure_iot_hub_defender_is_on", "text": "Enable **Defender for IoT** on all IoT Hubs and keep it `Enabled`. Route security data to a central workspace and your SIEM. Apply **least privilege** to IoT identities, enforce **network segmentation** and private access, and use **defense in depth** with continuous monitoring, alert tuning, and periodic coverage reviews."}}, "servicename": "defender", "checkaliases": [], "resourcetype": "microsoft.security/iotsecuritysolutions", "resourcegroup": "security", "additionalurls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/defender-for-iot/device-builders/quickstart-onboard-iot-hub", "https://support.icompaas.com/support/solutions/articles/62000229850-ensure-that-microsoft-defender-for-iot-hub-is-set-to-on-"], "subservicename": "", "resourceidtemplate": ""}	{}	01a00ec7-86e1-7a6c-8d5b-66e6a157f262	3e59acc5-3bdd-499e-8fd1-3e53b0a6ca47	2026-08-17 13:24:57.633496+05:30	f	{"NIS2": ["3.6.2", "6.9.2"], "SOC2": ["cc_3_1", "cc_3_2", "cc_4_2", "cc_6_8", "cc_7_1"], "C5-2025": ["OPS-04.01B"], "CIS-2.0": ["2.2.1"], "CIS-2.1": ["2.2.1"], "CIS-3.0": ["3.2.1"], "CIS-4.0": ["9.2.1"], "CIS-5.0": ["8.2.1"], "CIS-6.0": ["8.2.1"], "ENS-RD2022": ["mp.s.4.r1.az.nt.3"], "MITRE-ATTACK": ["T1190", "T1486", "T1499"], "ISO27001-2022": ["A.5.19", "A.5.21", "A.5.25", "A.5.28", "A.5.29", "A.8.7", "A.8.9"], "FedRAMP-20x-KSI-Low-25.05C": ["ksi-inr"]}	{global}	{defender}	{microsoft.security/iotsecuritysolutions}	\N	\N	{vulnerabilities}	security
01a00fa1-d243-7b3f-9637-c7c92b36699c	2026-08-17 17:40:58.501259+05:30	2026-08-17 17:40:58.501259+05:30	prowler-oraclecloud-audit_log_retention_period_365_days-ocid1.tenancy.oc1..aaaaaaaakgt7vtkpicqhxaxa2zs6qsiz7acdoot5jnylrzhvltdto2qrls7a-global-Audit Configuration	new	FAIL	Audit log retention period is 90 days (less than 365 days).	medium	medium	\N	{}	audit_log_retention_period_365_days	{"risk": "**Insufficient audit retention** or missing configuration shrinks the **detection window** and breaks **accountability**.\\n\\nEvidence for older actions may be unavailable, enabling attackers to evade detection, mask **data exfiltration**, and impede **forensic reconstruction** and compliance reporting.", "notes": "", "checkid": "audit_log_retention_period_365_days", "provider": "oraclecloud", "severity": "medium", "checktype": [], "dependson": [], "relatedto": [], "categories": ["logging", "forensics-ready"], "checktitle": "Tenancy audit log retention period is 365 days or greater", "compliance": {"SecNumCloud-3.2": ["10.4", "12.2", "12.6", "12.7", "14.2", "16.6"]}, "relatedurl": "", "description": "**OCI Audit configuration** defines tenancy-wide log retention for audit events. The finding evaluates whether the retention period (days) is `>= 365` and that an audit configuration exists, *applying across all regions and compartments*.", "remediation": {"code": {"cli": "oci audit configuration update --compartment-id <tenancy-ocid> --retention-period-days 365", "other": "1. Open the OCI Console and go to Governance & Administration > Audit\\n2. Click Configuration\\n3. Set Retention period (days) to 365\\n4. Click Save", "nativeiac": "", "terraform": "```hcl\\nresource \\"oci_audit_configuration\\" \\"<example_resource_name>\\" {\\n  compartment_id        = var.tenancy_ocid\\n  retention_period_days = 365 # Critical: sets audit log retention to 365 days to pass the check\\n}\\n```"}, "recommendation": {"url": "https://hub.prowler.com/check/audit_log_retention_period_365_days", "text": "Set audit retention to `>= 365` days at the tenancy level and protect the setting with **least privilege** and **separation of duties**.\\n\\nAdopt **defense in depth**: export audit logs to centralized, immutable storage or a SIEM for extended retention, integrity, and continuous monitoring."}}, "servicename": "audit", "checkaliases": [], "resourcetype": "Compartment", "resourcegroup": "governance", "additionalurls": ["https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/Audit/Tasks/settingretentionperiod.htm", "https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/tools/terraform-provider-oci/4.88.1/docs/r/audit_configuration.html"], "subservicename": "", "resourceidtemplate": ""}	{}	01a00fa1-9090-789e-9f57-b62772fab28a	3e59acc5-3bdd-499e-8fd1-3e53b0a6ca47	2026-08-17 17:40:58.499259+05:30	f	{"SecNumCloud-3.2": ["10.4", "12.2", "12.6", "12.7", "14.2", "16.6"]}	{global}	{audit}	{Compartment}	\N	\N	{logging,forensics-ready}	governance
01a00ec8-4654-7ab0-8a1c-b2213d868f3d	2026-08-17 13:43:21.366218+05:30	2026-08-17 13:43:21.366218+05:30	prowler-azure-iam_role_user_access_admin_restricted-ab5c336b-0e6b-4d8b-bf82-45cc005163e1-global-acd1492a-657f-4a4b-9cf4-8cc50751cb51	\N	PASS	Role assignment acd1492a-657f-4a4b-9cf4-8cc50751cb51 in subscription Azure subscription 1 (ab5c336b-0e6b-4d8b-bf82-45cc005163e1) does not grant User Access Administrator role.	high	high	\N	{}	iam_role_user_access_admin_restricted	{"risk": "Persistent `User Access Administrator` enables assigning high-privilege roles and reading control-plane data, enabling privilege escalation and unauthorized access. Impact: **confidentiality** (data exposure), **integrity** (unauthorized changes), **availability** (service disruption).", "notes": "", "checkid": "iam_role_user_access_admin_restricted", "provider": "azure", "severity": "high", "checktype": [], "dependson": [], "relatedto": [], "categories": ["identity-access"], "checktitle": "Role assignment does not grant the User Access Administrator role", "compliance": {"HIPAA": ["164_308_a_3_i", "164_308_a_3_ii_b", "164_308_a_4_i", "164_308_a_4_ii_b", "164_308_a_4_ii_c", "164_312_a_1"], "C5-2025": ["OIS-02.01B", "OIS-02.02B", "OIS-04.01B", "SP-01.04B", "PS-03.02B", "OPS-16.01B", "IAM-01.01B", "IAM-04.06B", "IAM-06.01B", "IAM-06.02B", "IAM-08.02B", "IAM-10.01B", "IAM-10.02B", "PSS-09.01AC"], "CIS-4.0": ["6.3.3"], "CIS-5.0": ["5.3.3"], "CIS-6.0": ["5.3.3"], "CCC-v2025.10": ["CCC.Core.CN05.AR01", "CCC.Core.CN05.AR02", "CCC.Core.CN05.AR06", "CCC.IAM.CN02.AR01", "CCC.IAM.CN02.AR02", "CCC.IAM.CN03.AR01", "CCC.IAM.CN03.AR02"], "SecNumCloud-3.2": ["9.1", "9.3"], "FedRAMP-20x-KSI-Low-25.05C": ["ksi-iam", "ksi-iam-07"], "RBI-Cyber-Security-Framework": ["annex_i_7_1"]}, "relatedurl": "", "description": "**Azure subscription role assignments** granting **User Access Administrator** are identified to surface principals able to manage access (`Azure RBAC`) at that scope.", "remediation": {"code": {"cli": "az role assignment delete --assignee <principal_id_or_upn> --role \\"User Access Administrator\\" --scope \\"/subscriptions/<subscription_id>\\"", "other": "1. In the Azure portal, go to Subscriptions and select <subscription>.\\n2. Open Access control (IAM) > Role assignments.\\n3. Filter by Role = User Access Administrator.\\n4. Select the assignment(s) and click Remove. Confirm.", "nativeiac": "", "terraform": ""}, "recommendation": {"url": "https://hub.prowler.com/check/iam_role_user_access_admin_restricted", "text": "Enforce **least privilege**:\\n- Avoid standing `User Access Administrator`; use time-bound, approval-based elevation (PIM)\\n- Scope access to only required subscriptions/resource groups\\n- Require MFA and monitor role activity\\n- Review regularly and remove unused grants"}}, "servicename": "iam", "checkaliases": [], "resourcetype": "microsoft.authorization/roleassignments", "resourcegroup": "IAM", "additionalurls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/elevate-access-global-admin?tabs=azure-portal%2Centra-audit-logs", "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/built-in-roles/privileged#user-access-administrator"], "subservicename": "", "resourceidtemplate": ""}	{}	01a00ec7-86e1-7a6c-8d5b-66e6a157f262	3e59acc5-3bdd-499e-8fd1-3e53b0a6ca47	2026-08-17 13:25:03.94344+05:30	f	{"HIPAA": ["164_308_a_3_i", "164_308_a_3_ii_b", "164_308_a_4_i", "164_308_a_4_ii_b", "164_308_a_4_ii_c", "164_312_a_1"], "C5-2025": ["OIS-02.01B", "OIS-02.02B", "OIS-04.01B", "SP-01.04B", "PS-03.02B", "OPS-16.01B", "IAM-01.01B", "IAM-04.06B", "IAM-06.01B", "IAM-06.02B", "IAM-08.02B", "IAM-10.01B", "IAM-10.02B", "PSS-09.01AC"], "CIS-4.0": ["6.3.3"], "CIS-5.0": ["5.3.3"], "CIS-6.0": ["5.3.3"], "CCC-v2025.10": ["CCC.Core.CN05.AR01", "CCC.Core.CN05.AR02", "CCC.Core.CN05.AR06", "CCC.IAM.CN02.AR01", "CCC.IAM.CN02.AR02", "CCC.IAM.CN03.AR01", "CCC.IAM.CN03.AR02"], "SecNumCloud-3.2": ["9.1", "9.3"], "FedRAMP-20x-KSI-Low-25.05C": [